var ACG_TAKES={"Dashboard\u00b7Credit Card Processing\u00b74D":"Solid. Flat-rate with no per-user charges is a real differentiator \u2014 practices hate surprise billing. Touch-screen terminal support is a plus for front desk flow.","Dashboard\u00b7Credit Card Processing\u00b7Nextech w/ P+":"Nextech Payments is genuinely good \u2014 one-click reconciliation and the ~35-minute month-end close is real. If they\u2019re on Nextech this is the right move.","Dashboard\u00b7Credit Card Processing\u00b7Nextech Cloud":"Same as P+ on payments. Strong integrated reconciliation. Recommend pairing with Nextech Payments at implementation.","Dashboard\u00b7Credit Card Processing\u00b7Symplast":"Clean and mobile-friendly. Works well for medspa workflows. No complaints here.","Dashboard\u00b7Credit Card Processing\u00b7ModMed":"Solid. Automated payment notifications are a good front desk time-saver.","Dashboard\u00b7Cash Pay Workflow\u00b74D":"4D was built for cash-pay aesthetics \u2014 this shows. Clean quoting-to-payment flow with no workarounds. Good fit for plastic surgery and medspa practices that don\u2019t do insurance.","Dashboard\u00b7Cash Pay Workflow\u00b7Nextech w/ P+":"Strong for hybrid practices. The ability to generate elective bills from EHR codes is valuable for plastic surgery. Recommend for any practice doing both insurance and cash-pay.","Dashboard\u00b7Cash Pay Workflow\u00b7Symplast":"Purpose-built for cash-pay aesthetics. Easy invoicing shortcuts are staff-friendly. Good choice for pure medspa or injector practices.","Dashboard\u00b7Cash Pay Workflow\u00b7ModMed":"Solid cash-pay support. Self-pay option in patient chart is clean. Good for surgical practices.","Dashboard\u00b7Packages & Bundles\u00b7Nextech w/ P+":"P+ has the most comprehensive package and spa management on this list per vendor claims. Worth verifying in a demo \u2014 but this is a real strength for medspa add-ons within a surgical practice.","Dashboard\u00b7Packages & Bundles\u00b7Symplast":"Strong package management \u2014 this is a Symplast sweet spot for injector and medspa practices. Works the way front desks actually think about bundled services.","Dashboard\u00b7Packages & Bundles\u00b74D":"Built in and functional. Good for medspa package tracking across visits.","Dashboard\u00b7Inventory Management\u00b74D":"Functional but requires setup knowledge to connect packages to services correctly. Walkthrough this carefully during implementation \u2014 the correlation between packages and staff services isn\u2019t obvious. No extra charge is a plus.","Dashboard\u00b7Inventory Management\u00b7Symplast":"Best for injector practices specifically \u2014 unit-level tracking for toxins and fillers is well done. If they\u2019re a high-volume injector practice, this matters.","Dashboard\u00b7Inventory Management\u00b7ModMed":"Solid inventory module integrated with POS. Worth demoing for practices with significant retail operations.","Dashboard\u00b7Loyalty Programs\u00b74D":"There\u2019s a workaround but it\u2019s exactly that \u2014 a workaround. If loyalty programs are central to the practice\u2019s growth strategy, this isn\u2019t the right platform for it.","Dashboard\u00b7Loyalty Programs\u00b7Symplast":"Best-in-class for aesthetics loyalty. In-app gift cards and targeted campaigns are genuinely differentiated. If loyalty is a priority, Symplast wins this category.","Dashboard\u00b7Loyalty Programs\u00b7Nextech w/ P+":"Marketing automation supports retention but there\u2019s no true loyalty points system. If loyalty programs are important, they\u2019ll need a third-party tool.","Dashboard\u00b7Quotes & Prepayment\u00b74D":"Quote versioning and electronic signing from any device are genuinely useful \u2014 especially for surgical consultations. Good workflow for high-value procedures.","Dashboard\u00b7Quotes & Prepayment\u00b7Nextech w/ P+":"Comprehensive quoting well-integrated into the EHR. The consult-to-booking workflow is solid for surgical practices.","Dashboard\u00b7Reporting & Analytics\u00b74D":"The ASPS data reporting integration is a hidden gem \u2014 automatic deidentified reporting at no extra cost. Good for practices that are ASPS members.","Dashboard\u00b7Reporting & Analytics\u00b7Nextech w/ P+":"Reporting is a real weakness in P+. If detailed analytics matter to this practice, push them toward Nextech Cloud or plan for a third-party BI tool. Don\u2019t oversell this.","Dashboard\u00b7Reporting & Analytics\u00b7Nextech Cloud":"Advanced Analytics is where Nextech Cloud earns its price premium over P+. Real-time visual dashboards are genuinely useful for practice managers.","Dashboard\u00b7Reporting & Analytics\u00b7ModMed":"Black Book #1 ranking is real. Reporting can be clunky to run but the underlying data is solid. AI-assisted reporting will improve this \u2014 worth watching.","Dashboard\u00b7Procedure Consents (Digital)\u00b74D":"The consent setup is a significant lift \u2014 everything has to be a Word document and loaded manually. Budget time and resources for this at implementation. The ASPS integration for $275 one-time is worth it.","Dashboard\u00b7Procedure Consents (Digital)\u00b7Nextech w/ P+":"Same heavy lift as 4D \u2014 Word documents required, manual upload. The ASPS $275 integration is worth the investment. Plan this as a project, not a feature.","Dashboard\u00b7Procedure Consents (Digital)\u00b7Nextech Cloud":"Same consent setup requirements as P+. Treat this as a dedicated implementation project. ASPS integration recommended.","Dashboard\u00b7Procedure Consents (Digital)\u00b7Symplast":"The 7-14 day lead time through the Dev Team is a real bottleneck. Plan consent library build-out well before go-live. Don\u2019t assume this is day-one ready.","Dashboard\u00b7Procedure Consents (Digital)\u00b7ModMed":"Klara makes this more complex than it should be. The 14-21 day lead time to get forms into Klara is a real constraint \u2014 this is a HUGE undertaking. Set expectations early and start the content project before implementation begins.","Dashboard\u00b7Injectable Documentation\u00b74D":"Solid for unit tracking with diagrams, but the gap between chart note and inventory is a real workflow issue. Units entered on the chart don\u2019t automatically pull into charges or inventory. Workaround-dependent.","Dashboard\u00b7Injectable Documentation\u00b7Nextech w/ P+":"Strong documentation with templates but same gap as 4D \u2014 units don\u2019t auto-pull into charges like Cloud does. If this practice is high-volume injectors, push toward Cloud.","Dashboard\u00b7Injectable Documentation\u00b7Nextech Cloud":"Best Nextech option for injectors. Unit mapping to checkout is the key differentiator over P+. Recommend Cloud over P+ for any injector-heavy practice.","Dashboard\u00b7Injectable Documentation\u00b7Symplast":"Excellent for injector practices. Drawing tools are aesthetics-specific and the unit tracking works the way injectors actually think. Strong recommendation for medspa/injector practices.","Dashboard\u00b7Injectable Documentation\u00b7ModMed":"Adaptive learning for dosing preferences is genuinely useful for high-volume providers. Good for surgical practices with regular injection days.","Dashboard\u00b7AI Scribe / Voice-to-Text\u00b74D":"At $175/provider/month for a basic tool, this is hard to justify. No template customization is a real limitation. ModMed Scribe or Doximity DoxGPT are better options if AI documentation is a priority.","Dashboard\u00b7AI Scribe / Voice-to-Text\u00b7Symplast":"Flag the data storage concern to clients \u2014 recordings and transcripts being stored could be a legal liability. Get clarity from Symplast on their data retention policy before recommending.","Dashboard\u00b7AI Scribe / Voice-to-Text\u00b7ModMed":"Best-in-class for plastic surgery. Trained on 750M+ encounters with specialty-specific language. If AI documentation is a priority, ModMed is the answer. Worth a significant conversation during sales.","Dashboard\u00b7Surgical & OR Scheduling\u00b74D":"Well-integrated for surgical workflow \u2014 quotes, prepayments, and closing surgery all connect cleanly. The pre-op checklist limitation (can\u2019t assign to individuals) is a gap \u2014 practices end up using Teams/Planner for this.","Dashboard\u00b7Surgical & OR Scheduling\u00b7Nextech w/ P+":"Comprehensive but the pre-op checklist gap is real \u2014 most practices end up in Teams or Planner for surgical prep management. Plan for this workaround.","Dashboard\u00b7Surgical & OR Scheduling\u00b7ModMed":"Remembering preferred techniques, implant specs, and anesthesia settings is a genuine time-saver for high-volume surgical practices. This is a real selling point for surgical practices.","Dashboard\u00b7Telehealth & Virtual Consults\u00b74D":"The notification link not being sent until appointment time is a real problem for patient experience. Providers complain about this. Worth flagging in demo \u2014 ask if they\u2019ve resolved it.","Dashboard\u00b7Telehealth & Virtual Consults\u00b7Symplast":"Mobile-first telehealth that actually works from a phone is genuinely useful. Good for practices that want to do virtual consultations without a separate platform.","Dashboard\u00b7Online Booking\u00b7Nextech w/ P+":"The setup is tedious \u2014 requires correct appointment types and templates to be built out first. This is an implementation project, not a feature you turn on. Plan the appointment type matrix before go-live.","Dashboard\u00b7Online Booking\u00b7Nextech Cloud":"Same setup requirements as P+. Appointment type matrix needs to be designed and built before this works properly. Worth the investment \u2014 no-show alerts and one-click rebooking pay off.","Dashboard\u00b7Online Patient Portal\u00b74D":"Not a true portal \u2014 patients can\u2019t log in and access chart notes. It\u2019s really a health history and consent collection tool. Be careful how this is presented to clients.","Dashboard\u00b7Online Patient Portal\u00b7Nextech w/ P+":"The portal exists and is functional but the patient-facing UI is dated. Don\u2019t lead with this in a demo. It\u2019s a weak point.","Dashboard\u00b7Online Patient Portal\u00b7Symplast":"The patient app is the real differentiator here \u2014 not just a portal but a mobile experience patients actually use. Good for practices that want to differentiate on patient engagement.","Dashboard\u00b72-Way Text Messaging\u00b74D":"The native texting has real limitations \u2014 no photo support and weak notifications. Most practices pair 4D with Weave for actual 2-way texting. Budget for this add-on.","Dashboard\u00b72-Way Text Messaging\u00b7Nextech w/ P+":"Most Nextech practices end up using a phone system (Weave, Podium) for actual 2-way texting \u2014 the native feature is limited. See the Phone Systems tab for the better conversation.","Dashboard\u00b7Appointment Reminders (SMS/Email)\u00b7Symplast":"The built-in reminder types are limited and hard to configure without understanding the system well. Training on this specifically before go-live is essential.","Dashboard\u00b7Appointment Reminders (SMS/Email)\u00b7ModMed":"The Klara integration for reminders is not fully clear in terms of workflow. Get a clear demo of the end-to-end reminder flow before committing to this setup.","Dashboard\u00b7CRM & Lead Management\u00b74D":"Basic is the right word. Fine for a practice that isn\u2019t doing active marketing, but any practice focused on growth needs a dedicated CRM on top of 4D.","Dashboard\u00b7CRM & Lead Management\u00b7Nextech w/ P+":"The native CRM is newer and worth demoing. If it delivers on the 100% lead capture claim, this is a meaningful upgrade. Verify in a live demo before recommending as a replacement for a dedicated CRM.","Dashboard\u00b7CRM & Lead Management\u00b7Symplast":"The 118% lead growth claim is from a real client case. The built-in CRM is genuinely useful for aesthetics practices. Good differentiator for growth-focused practices.","Dashboard\u00b7Patient Reviews & Reputation\u00b7Podium":"This is Podium\u2019s original core product and they\u2019re still the best at it. If a practice\u2019s biggest pain point is Google reviews, Podium is the answer \u2014 full stop.","Dashboard\u00b7Digital Intake Forms\u00b7Nextech w/ P+":"Build-out required means staff time upfront. This is an implementation project. Don\u2019t assume it works out of the box.","Dashboard\u00b7Digital Intake Forms\u00b7Symplast":"One of the best native intake experiences on this list \u2014 customizable, HIPAA-secure, reduces front desk time meaningfully. Good to highlight in demos.","Dashboard\u00b7Patient Communication (Klara, Luma)\u00b7ModMed":"Klara + ModMed is genuinely one of the best patient communication combinations available for plastic surgery. If they\u2019re on ModMed and not using Klara, this is an easy conversation to have.","Dashboard\u00b7Implementation Timeline\u00b74D":"Month-to-month with free data migration is the strongest commercial positioning on this list. For any practice nervous about commitment, lead with this. $650/mo starting is transparent and reasonable.","Dashboard\u00b7Implementation Timeline\u00b7Nextech w/ P+":"The auto-renewing contract issue is real and comes up consistently in user reviews. Before a client signs with Nextech, have them review the auto-renewal terms carefully and request a clear cancellation process in writing.","Dashboard\u00b7Implementation Timeline\u00b7Nextech Cloud":"Same contract concern as P+. The 48-hour downtime for switchover needs to be planned carefully \u2014 coordinate with the practice administrator well in advance.","Dashboard\u00b7Implementation Timeline\u00b7Symplast":"Easy to implement and the sales team is responsive, but some clients have reported aggressive sales tactics around contract terms. Coach clients to take time before signing.","Dashboard\u00b7Implementation Timeline\u00b7ModMed":"Enterprise-grade implementation with plastic surgery staff handling it is genuinely valuable \u2014 not DIY like some platforms. The MOMENTUM conference is a real resource. Best for established practices willing to invest in a full deployment.","Dashboard\u00b7Contract Flexibility\u00b7Nextech w/ P+":"AUTO-RENEWAL IS A MAJOR WATCH-OUT. Multiple clients have been caught by this. Always flag the contract terms before a client signs. Request a written cancellation process.","Dashboard\u00b7Contract Flexibility\u00b74D":"Best contract terms on this list \u2014 period. Month-to-month with no per-user fees and no annual maintenance. This is a real differentiator to lead with when price or commitment is a concern.","Dashboard\u00b7Pricing Transparency\u00b74D":"Best transparency on this list. $650/mo starting, no hidden fees. Makes budgeting conversations easy.","Dashboard\u00b7Pricing Transparency\u00b7Nextech w/ P+":"Not transparent and clients consistently report being charged for things they didn\u2019t expect. Always request a full itemized quote and ask specifically about add-on fees before signing.","Dashboard\u00b7Pricing Transparency\u00b7ModMed":"Custom quotes only and some clients report variance between initial quote and final cost. Push for an itemized quote and reference pricing in the contract.","Dashboard\u00b7User Rating (G2 / Capterra)\u00b74D":"Built by Dr. Robert Pollack, a practicing plastic surgeon \u2014 the workflows reflect that. The ASPS partnership and month-to-month pricing make this worth serious consideration for smaller or newer practices.","Dashboard\u00b7User Rating (G2 / Capterra)\u00b7Nextech w/ P+":"239 reviews is a solid sample. The auto-renewing contract complaint is consistent across negative reviews \u2014 this is a real pattern, not an outlier. Flag it every time.","Dashboard\u00b7User Rating (G2 / Capterra)\u00b7Symplast":"4.4/5 on Capterra is strong. Founded by plastic surgeons with 3,500+ users. The mobile-first approach is a real differentiator. Sales process concerns are worth noting but don\u2019t outweigh the platform strengths.","Dashboard\u00b7User Rating (G2 / Capterra)\u00b7ModMed":"10 consecutive years as #1 by Black Book is meaningful validation. The reporting limitations are real but the overall platform quality is consistently high.","Dashboard\u00b7Lab Integrations\u00b74D":"Lab integrations are expensive and complicated across ALL platforms \u2014 not just 4D. The realistic workflow is custom forms plus scan/fax back. Use internal tasks to track. Set this expectation with clients early.","Dashboard\u00b7Lab Integrations\u00b7Nextech Cloud":"Nextech Cloud has the most developed lab integration workflow on this list with step-by-step staff guidance. If lab integration is a real priority, Cloud has an edge.","Dashboard\u00b7Canfield\u00b74D":"The webhook-based integration requires a download running on the computer \u2014 this is fragile and worth flagging. Ask the client if they\u2019re already using Canfield and verify the integration is stable before committing.","Dashboard\u00b7Open API / Webhooks\u00b7ModMed":"FHIR-certified API is the gold standard for healthcare interoperability. If they have other systems that need to integrate, ModMed\u2019s API is the most enterprise-ready on this list.","Dashboard\u00b7Mobile App (iOS & Android)\u00b74D":"No dedicated mobile app is a real limitation for providers who want to chart or review schedules from their phone. Browser-based works but it\u2019s not the same experience.","Dashboard\u00b7Mobile App (iOS & Android)\u00b7Symplast":"Mobile-first is Symplast\u2019s real differentiator. If the provider wants to run the practice from their phone, this is the answer. Don\u2019t underestimate how much this matters to younger providers.","Dashboard\u00b7Mobile App (iOS & Android)\u00b7ModMed":"iPad-native design is genuinely excellent \u2014 the PocketEMA app is well-designed. Best for providers who want a tablet-first clinical experience.","CRM Comparison\u00b7Parent Platform / Vendor\u00b7Nextech CRM":"Native to Nextech \u2014 no integration overhead. If they're already on Nextech and want CRM, start here before looking at third-party options.","CRM Comparison\u00b7Parent Platform / Vendor\u00b7SymplastCRM":"Native to Symplast. Best CRM option for Symplast practices \u2014 no middleware, shared database, and the pipeline stages auto-update from EHR actions.","CRM Comparison\u00b7Parent Platform / Vendor\u00b7Zone DM":"The fully managed option. Best for practices that don't want to configure or run a CRM themselves. Agency does everything \u2014 sequences, campaigns, reporting. Higher cost but lower staff burden.","CRM Comparison\u00b7Parent Platform / Vendor\u00b7Dewy":"Best CRM for ModMed practices. Native direct API \u2014 no Zapier, no middleware. The Practice Voice Engine writes nurture sequences in your voice. Strong for lapsed patient reactivation.","CRM Comparison\u00b7Parent Platform / Vendor\u00b7Aesthetix CRM":"Works across Nextech, ModMed, and 4D. Good middle ground between native and standalone. Keragon middleware is reliable but adds a layer to maintain.","CRM Comparison\u00b7Contract Flexibility\u00b7Zone DM":"Month-to-month is a real advantage \u2014 you can exit if performance doesn't deliver. Hold them accountable to lead conversion metrics from day one.","CRM Comparison\u00b7Contract Flexibility\u00b7Dewy":"Month-to-month at $319/mo is transparent and fair for what you get. Low risk to try.","CRM Comparison\u00b7Done-For-You Setup\u00b7Zone DM":"Zone builds everything for you \u2014 sequences, campaigns, tracking. This is the right call for practices that don't have a marketing-savvy staff member. Fully hands-off once live.","CRM Comparison\u00b7Done-For-You Setup\u00b7Dewy":"Dewy writes your nurture sequences for you. This is a meaningful differentiator \u2014 most CRMs give you templates, Dewy gives you actual content written for your practice.","CRM Comparison\u00b7AI-Powered Nurture Sequences\u00b7Nextech CRM":"Nextech Cora AI is newer. Worth demoing but not yet as proven as dedicated CRM platforms. Verify in a live demo with real sequences before recommending.","CRM Comparison\u00b7Weaknesses / Watch-outs\u00b7Nextech CRM":"New product \u2014 limited real-world reviews outside Nextech's own marketing. Request client references specifically for the CRM module before recommending.","CRM Comparison\u00b7Weaknesses / Watch-outs\u00b7SymplastCRM":"Twilio SMS is billed per message \u2014 costs can add up for high-volume practices. Get a clear estimate based on their patient volume before committing.","CRM Comparison\u00b7Weaknesses / Watch-outs\u00b7Podium AI OS":"New EMR layer \u2014 CRM depth is unproven for practices with complex clinical needs. Pre/post-op clinical content delivery needs verification in a real demo.","CRM Comparison\u00b7Weaknesses / Watch-outs\u00b7Zone DM":"Quality depends heavily on the team assigned. Ask to meet the actual people who will work the account before signing. Get performance metrics in the contract.","CRM Comparison\u00b7Weaknesses / Watch-outs\u00b7Aesthetix CRM":"Keragon middleware adds a layer that can break. Verify bidirectional sync depth for their specific EMR before recommending.","CRM Comparison\u00b7Best Fit Practice Type\u00b7Zone DM":"Best for practices that want fully managed marketing with no internal marketing staff. Any EMR. Good starting point for practices that don't know what CRM they want yet.","CRM Comparison\u00b7Best Fit Practice Type\u00b7Dewy":"ModMed, Zenoti, DrChrono, and Meevo practices. If they're on ModMed and don't have a CRM, Dewy is the first call.","Phone Systems\u00b74D EMR \u2014 Native Integration\u00b7Weave":"Weave is the gold standard for 4D practices. Call pop, schedule sync, 2-way texting, and review requests all connect natively. If they're on 4D, Weave is the phone system recommendation \u2014 full stop.","Phone Systems\u00b7Nextech \u2014 Native Integration\u00b7Weave":"Same as 4D \u2014 Weave + Nextech is a proven combination. Schedule sync and call pop work reliably. Recommend Weave first for any Nextech practice evaluating phone systems.","Phone Systems\u00b7Call Pop (patient ID on ring)\u00b7Weave":"Weave Call Pop is best-in-class for aesthetics. Staff sees patient name, upcoming appointment, and last visit before answering. Changes how the front desk operates.","Phone Systems\u00b7Call Pop (patient ID on ring)\u00b7RingCentral":"RingCentral has call pop but it's more complex to configure. Weave does this better for smaller aesthetics practices.","Phone Systems\u00b7Missed Call Auto-Text\u00b7Weave":"One of Weave's best features for aesthetics \u2014 missed call triggers automatic text to the patient. Captures leads that would otherwise be lost. Practices see immediate impact.","Phone Systems\u00b7Missed Call Auto-Text\u00b7Podium Phones":"Strong missed-call texting. Podium's bread and butter. Works well but consider the full Podium ecosystem costs before committing.","Phone Systems\u00b7SMS Marketing Campaigns\u00b7Weave":"Weave's SMS campaigns work well for appointment reminders and promotions. Not as sophisticated as a dedicated CRM but good enough for practices not ready for full CRM investment.","Phone Systems\u00b7Real-Time Call Coaching (AI)\u00b7Dialpad":"Dialpad's AI call coaching is genuinely impressive \u2014 real-time transcription with coaching cues during the call. Good for practices investing in front desk training and conversion optimization.","Phone Systems\u00b7Overall Rating (G2/Capterra)\u00b7Weave":"4.5/5 is strong and consistent. Weave reviews specifically highlight the healthcare workflow integration as the differentiator. Negative reviews are mostly about pricing.","Phone Systems\u00b7Overall Rating (G2/Capterra)\u00b7RingCentral":"4.0/5 is solid for a general business phone system. Reviews note it's more complex to set up than Weave. Better for larger multi-location practices with IT support.","Phone Systems\u00b7Pricing (approx/user/mo)\u00b7Weave":"At $40-75/user it's higher than competitors, but the value is in the EMR integration \u2014 if that's not being used, the price is hard to justify. Negotiate based on user count.","Phone Systems\u00b7HIPAA Compliance + BAA Available\u00b7Weave":"All major phone systems on this list offer a BAA. Never skip this step \u2014 get it signed before go-live regardless of which system you choose.","Phone Systems\u00b7Implementation Timeline\u00b7Weave":"2-4 weeks is accurate. Weave onboarding is straightforward. The EMR integration configuration is where practices spend the most time \u2014 plan for it.","Phone Systems\u00b7Dedicated Healthcare Support\u00b7Weave":"Weave's healthcare-specific support team is a real differentiator. They understand practice workflows, not just phone systems. Worth something when you're troubleshooting at 8am before clinic.","Patient Financing\u00b7Overall ACG Pick\u00b7Cherry":"Cherry rounds out the ACG financing stack as the approval gap filler. When patients don't qualify for CareCredit, Cherry's 80%+ approval rate with soft credit check closes the case. Free to add, no contract, and the All\u0113 integration is a bonus for Allergan product practices. Every practice should have all three \u2014 CareCredit, PatientFi, and Cherry \u2014 because patients have different needs and credit profiles.","Patient Financing\u00b7Overall ACG Pick\u00b7CareCredit":"CareCredit leads the ACG financing conversation. Patients already have it \u2014 they use it for vets, dentists, and other healthcare. The EMR integration is now strong across most platforms. Yes, the fees are higher and the deferred interest is a real patient complaint, but brand recognition and existing cardholders make it the natural first conversation. Lead with CareCredit, add PatientFi for high-cost cases, and keep Cherry for patients who don't qualify for the other two.","Patient Financing\u00b7Overall ACG Pick\u00b7PatientFi":"PatientFi is essential for high-cost surgical cases. Mommy makeovers, rhinoplasty with multiple procedures, full body contouring \u2014 these are the cases where you need PatientFi. One watch-out: new startup practices have transaction limits until they establish tier status, so set that expectation early. Once established, PatientFi fills the gap that CareCredit and Cherry can't reach.","Patient Financing\u00b7Deferred Interest Risk\u00b7CareCredit":"Deferred interest is the single biggest patient complaint about CareCredit. If a patient doesn't pay off the full balance before the promo period ends, they get charged all the interest retroactively. Practices lose patient trust over this. Make sure staff explains it clearly at point of sale.","Patient Financing\u00b7Credit Score Impact\u00b7Cherry":"Soft credit check is a major patient-facing advantage. Patients who are nervous about their credit score will appreciate that applying for Cherry doesn't hurt their score. Front desk should lead with this.","Patient Financing\u00b7Approval Rate\u00b7Cherry":"80-90% approval including the Pay-in-4 option (capped around $3,500). For larger amounts the approval rate drops but is still above CareCredit. The key talking point: more patients get approved, more cases get closed.","Patient Financing\u00b7All\u0113 / Allergan Integration\u00b7Cherry":"Cherry's All\u0113 partnership is unique \u2014 allows Allergan product financing through Cherry. If the practice sells Botox, Juvederm, Kybella, or other Allergan products, this is a meaningful differentiator. No other financing partner has this.","Patient Financing\u00b7Best For High-Cost Surgical Cases\u00b7PatientFi":"PatientFi is the right answer for practices doing high-cost procedures \u2014 mommy makeovers, extensive body contouring, rhinoplasty with additional procedures. Fills the gap when Cherry's $50K cap isn't enough.","Patient Financing\u00b7Max Loan Amount\u00b7PatientFi":"Up to $85K+ is genuinely differentiated for plastics. No other financing option on this list gets there. For surgical practices with high-value cases, PatientFi belongs in the financing conversation.","Patient Financing\u00b7True 0% APR Available\u00b7Cherry":"Cherry's 0% APR is real \u2014 not deferred interest. Patients pay off the balance over the promo period with no interest charged at all if they complete payments. Fundamentally different from CareCredit's deferred interest model.","Patient Financing\u00b7Setup Cost\u00b7Cherry":"Free to add with no contract. This removes every barrier to offering it. There's no reason a practice should be going without Cherry in 2026.","Patient Financing\u00b7Best For New / Startup Practices\u00b7Cherry":"For startups, add Cherry immediately \u2014 it's free, no contract, and gets them offering financing on day one. Add CareCredit next. Hold on PatientFi until the practice is established and past the tier limits. Every practice should eventually have all three.","Imaging & Photography\u00b7Primary Use Case\u00b7Touch MD":"Touch MD is the patient education tool \u2014 it's about the consult experience, not photo management. Best for injectable practices and medspa that want to show patients what's possible during a consultation.","Imaging & Photography\u00b7Primary Use Case\u00b7Canfield VECTRA":"VECTRA is the gold standard for surgical simulation. If a practice does breast augmentation, rhinoplasty, or body contouring and wants to show patients a 3D preview, VECTRA is the answer. Significant hardware investment but proven consult conversion impact.","Imaging & Photography\u00b7Primary Use Case\u00b7Image Assist":"Image Assist is the Nextech-native photo management solution. If they're on Nextech, this is the path of least resistance for organized before/after management. Included in Nextech contract.","Imaging & Photography\u00b7Primary Use Case\u00b7Canfield Mirror":"Mirror is the photo management platform \u2014 not simulation. Great for organized before/after archives and MatchPose overlay technology. Lower cost than VECTRA for practices that don't need 3D simulation.","Imaging & Photography\u00b7Primary Use Case\u00b7VISIA Complexion":"VISIA is the skin analysis tool \u2014 completely different use case from surgical simulation. Best for medical aesthetics practices that do skin treatments and want objective measurements to show progress.","Imaging & Photography\u00b73D Simulation\u00b7Canfield VECTRA":"VECTRA XT is the industry standard for breast augmentation simulation. Practices that use it consistently report higher consult conversion rates. The ROI conversation is straightforward \u2014 one or two additional cases per month pays for the system.","Imaging & Photography\u00b7Best For High-Volume Surgical Practice\u00b7Canfield VECTRA":"VECTRA is the answer for surgical practices. The XT model for breast, the M3 for face and rhinoplasty. High upfront cost ($30-80K hardware) but practices that invest in it don't look back.","Imaging & Photography\u00b7Best For Budget-Conscious Practice\u00b7Image Assist":"If they're on Nextech, Image Assist is included \u2014 free. No additional cost for organized photo management and basic before/after. Start here before spending on additional imaging tools.","Imaging & Photography\u00b7Best For Injectable / Medspa Focus\u00b7Touch MD":"Touch MD is the right call for injectable and medspa practices. iPad-native, patient-facing, designed for the consult experience. Helps injectors show patients what treatments are possible and set realistic expectations.","Imaging & Photography\u00b7Best For Patient Engagement\u00b7Touch MD":"Touch MD was specifically designed for patient-facing education during the consultation. The ROI is in consult conversion \u2014 patients who understand their options say yes more often.","Imaging & Photography\u00b7Consult-to-Booking Conversion Impact\u00b7Canfield VECTRA":"Multiple studies and anecdotal evidence from practices consistently show VECTRA improves surgical consult conversion. Patients who see a 3D simulation of their outcome are more likely to book. Hard to quantify but consistently reported.","Imaging & Photography\u00b7Mobile / iPad Use\u00b7Touch MD":"iPad-native is Touch MD's core design principle. The consult experience is built around handing the iPad to the patient. Works on Canon Connect for standardized photography.","Imaging & Photography\u00b7Approx. Starting Cost\u00b7Canfield VECTRA":"The hardware investment is real \u2014 $30-80K depending on configuration. For high-volume surgical practices this ROI is clear. For lower-volume practices, start with Mirror for photo management and evaluate VECTRA when volume justifies it.","Imaging & Photography\u00b7Approx. Starting Cost\u00b7Touch MD":"The package pricing ($600-$200/month depending on tier) is accessible. Start with the base package and upgrade as the practice sees value. No hardware cost.","Imaging & Photography\u00b7Approx. Starting Cost\u00b7Image Assist":"$250/month is reasonable for organized photo management, but verify whether it's included in the Nextech contract \u2014 for many Nextech practices it is.","Phone Systems\u00b7Bi-directional Data Sync\u00b7Weave":"The killer feature nobody talks about enough: in 4D and ModMed, Weave writes appointment status changes back into the EMR automatically. Staff never has to open Weave to update a status \u2014 it just happens. That's the conversation to have when demoing Weave for these practices. Also \u2014 fax number porting into 4D is a hidden gem for practices transitioning off a traditional fax line.","Phone Systems\u00b74D EMR \u2014 Native Integration\u00b7Weave":"The gold standard for 4D practices. Bi-directional appointment status sync writes back to the EMR without staff ever touching Weave. Call pop, missed call auto-text, review requests, fax porting \u2014 everything connects natively. If they're on 4D, Weave is the recommendation full stop.","Phone Systems\u00b7ModMed \u2014 Native Integration\u00b7Weave":"Same bi-directional status sync as 4D \u2014 appointment updates write back to ModMed automatically. Weave + ModMed is a strong pairing for established surgical practices.","Phone Systems\u00b7Best Fit Practice Size\u00b7Dialpad":"ACG's top recommendation for plastic surgery startups. The price point is accessible, setup is fast, it works natively on the provider's cell phone, and the call reporting is genuinely useful for practice managers monitoring front desk performance. When a new practice can't justify Weave's price yet, Dialpad is the answer.","Phone Systems\u00b7AI Chat / Webchat\u00b7Podium Phones":"Podium Phones only makes sense inside the Podium ecosystem. Avery handling phone, text, and email in one trained AI is genuinely differentiated \u2014 but the market isn't ready for AI-answered calls at scale yet. The real value is Podium as CRM with phones added for the unified Avery layer. Without that context, the price is hard to justify against Weave's integration depth. No confirmed EMR integrations \u2014 expect this to narrow further as Podium pushes its own EMR.","Phone Systems\u00b7Contract Flexibility\u00b7RingCentral":"RingCentral is the only scenario where we'd consider it over Weave \u2014 Nextech Cloud practices where the integration is decent. Even then, compare it directly against Weave before recommending. Price is high, UI is underwhelming, and the contracts are long. Not a first call.","Phone Systems\u00b7Mobile App\u00b7Zoom Phone":"Zoom Phone only makes sense if the practice is already deep in the Zoom ecosystem for meetings. Most plastic surgery and medspa practices aren't \u2014 and there are better purpose-built options at every price point. Not a client recommendation.","Imaging & Photography\u00b7Primary Use Case\u00b7Touch MD":"Personal favorite for photography. Canon Connect with lighting setup creates a standardized photo environment that most practices don't have. The social media tagging and direct upload is unique \u2014 nobody else on this list does that. Coming in 2026: combined Nextech+TouchMD patient portal which will significantly change the value proposition for Nextech practices. Watch this space. Price point is high and support/implementation are lacking which shows in feature adoption \u2014 most practices aren't using half of what they're paying for.","Imaging & Photography\u00b7Patient-Facing Visualization\u00b7Touch MD":"The mirroring for before and afters is excellent. Main limitation: you can't change the sequencing for breast, body, etc. \u2014 it's fixed. No morphing capability either, so this isn't a simulation tool. For consult education and social media, it's strong. For surgical simulation, look at VECTRA.","Imaging & Photography\u00b7Best For Patient Engagement\u00b7Touch MD":"Social media tagging and direct upload to practice accounts is a genuine differentiator \u2014 no other imaging tool on this list does this. For practices that are building their social media presence with real patient content, this matters.","Imaging & Photography\u00b7EMR Integration\u00b74D EMR\u00b7Touch MD":"Strong integration. Canon Connect setup with lighting creates a standardized photo environment. Worth demoing specifically for 4D practices that want a professional photography workflow.","Imaging & Photography\u00b7Approx. Starting Cost\u00b7Image Assist":"$250/month with a 7-day free trial is the most accessible entry point on this list. Low risk to try. Canon Connect capabilities match TouchMD at a lower price. The ASPS partnership for procedure-specific photo layouts is actively funded and in development \u2014 this will be a significant differentiator when it ships. Honest caveat: early in ACG implementation so long-term support assessment is still pending.","Imaging & Photography\u00b7Before & After Photo Management\u00b7Image Assist":"The custom sequencing per body part is better than TouchMD \u2014 you can set your own order for breast, body, face rather than being locked into a fixed sequence. Strong for practices that want their own workflow. No social media upload is the main gap vs TouchMD.","Imaging & Photography\u00b7Best For Budget-Conscious Practice\u00b7Image Assist":"$250/month with 7-day free trial and Canon Connect. For any practice not on Nextech that wants a professional photo management workflow, Image Assist is the first recommendation. The ASPS-funded procedure-specific layouts coming soon will make this even stronger.","Imaging & Photography\u00b73D Simulation\u00b7Canfield VECTRA":"The only option on the market for facial plastics simulation. If a practice does facial plastics and wants to show patients a simulation of their outcome, VECTRA is the answer \u2014 nothing else competes. The conversation is simple: is simulation important to their consult process? If yes, VECTRA. If not, start with Mirror or Image Assist for photo management.","Imaging & Photography\u00b7Best For High-Volume Surgical Practice\u00b7Canfield VECTRA":"VECTRA for simulation, specifically facial plastics. Most practices use it for photo capture too but the real value is the simulation capability. Photos store on the practice's own server \u2014 4D and Nextech both have download features to pull them into the EMR database.","Imaging & Photography\u00b7Before & After Photo Management\u00b7Canfield Mirror":"ACG has limited real-world client experience with Mirror \u2014 one client only. Most practices in our client base are using it primarily for photo capture and storage, not the full feature set. Getting displaced by TouchMD and Image Assist. Verify current capabilities directly with Canfield before recommending.","Imaging & Photography\u00b7Skin Analysis & Complexion\u00b7VISIA Complexion":"ACG has limited real-world experience \u2014 one client only. Completely different use case from surgical simulation or photo management. Skin analysis for medical aesthetics practices doing laser, chemical peels, or skin treatments. If a practice is asking about VISIA specifically for that use case, verify current pricing and support directly. Not a primary ACG recommendation at this time.","Dashboard·2-Way Text Messaging·Symplast":"Symplast texting runs on GoHighLevel (GHL) powered by Twilio — per-message billing is real. Three things every Symplast practice needs before going live on texting: (1) A2P 10DLC registration is required — 3-7 business days for approval plus 24 hours for number association. Do not promise patients texts until this clears. (2) SMS activates separately from voice after a number port — expect 2-4 additional business days after voice is working. (3) Short-code messages like bank 2FA codes will NOT deliver to a GHL-managed number. Any staff using that number for personal banking must update those accounts first.","Dashboard·Appointment Reminders (SMS/Email)·Symplast":"Symplast reminder automation runs through GHL/Twilio. A2P 10DLC registration must be complete before automated messages go out — carriers will filter unregistered bulk SMS. Budget 3-7 business days for approval before go-live. New numbers also need to ramp up volume gradually — start with smaller batches and build sending history over the first few weeks.","CRM Comparison·SMS / Text Marketing·SymplastCRM":"Twilio per-message billing means costs scale with volume. Get a patient volume estimate before recommending. A2P 10DLC registration is required for any bulk texting and is non-negotiable — budget 3-7 business days for brand/campaign approval before the practice can send automated campaigns.","CRM Comparison·Integration Method·SymplastCRM":"Symplast CRM is GoHighLevel (GHL) white-labeled. This matters in practice for two reasons: (1) features GHL releases that Symplast has not yet surfaced may still be accessible — the VoIP deskphone SIP endpoint feature released August 31 2026 is a live example; (2) when troubleshooting phone or texting issues, the stack is GHL + Twilio + carriers — understanding this tells you exactly where a problem lives.","CRM Comparison·Weaknesses / Watch-outs·SymplastCRM":"Three watch-outs from Symplast's own telephony documentation: (1) Number porting takes 7-14 business days and can run longer — porting PINs can expire mid-process requiring resubmission. Never cancel existing service until the port is fully tested. (2) Calls may begin routing into the CRM before any confirmation is received — staff need to know this. (3) Personal numbers ported into Symplast become business numbers — all calls and texts flow into the CRM and may be visible to staff. Providers using a personal cell as a business line need to understand this. Also: Symplast's own guideline says no hardphone support, but GHL added VoIP deskphone SIP endpoint support August 31 2026 — ask Symplast support about this if a client wants physical phones.","CRM Comparison·Parent Platform / Vendor·SymplastCRM":"Update August 31 2026: GoHighLevel (the platform powering Symplast) now supports native VoIP deskphone SIP endpoint via LeadConnector. Symplast's own guideline still states no hardphone support — that document predates this release. Practices wanting physical deskphones should ask Symplast support specifically about SIP endpoint configuration through GHL. Proven hardware: Yealink T54W, Poly VVX 450, Grandstream GXP 2170. One deskphone per LC user. Blind transfers only — warm transfer not yet supported. $0.10 per deskphone call transfer (SIP Refer)."};
// ── AESTHETICSPRO ACG TAKES (added after ACG_TAKES definition) ───────────────
ACG_TAKES["Dashboard·User Rating (G2 / Capterra)·AestheticsPro"]="Solid for medspa. Wrong for surgical plastics. If the practice is medspa-first with no surgical caseload, AestheticsPro is worth serious consideration -- it covers the whole operation in one platform at a reasonable price. If there is any surgical volume, rule it out.";
ACG_TAKES["Dashboard·Digital Intake Forms·AestheticsPro"]="500+ pre-built forms is the headline differentiator here. Every other platform on this list requires you to build or upload your own. For a new medspa that does not want to spend 40 hours building forms from scratch, this is a meaningful time save.";
ACG_TAKES["Dashboard·Insurance Billing·AestheticsPro"]="Hard no for any practice with insurance volume. AestheticsPro is cash-pay only by design. This is not a limitation -- it is a feature for the right practice. But verify early.";
ACG_TAKES["Dashboard·Memberships·AestheticsPro"]="One of the stronger membership implementations on this list. If the practice is building a recurring revenue model around memberships, AestheticsPro handles it natively and well.";


